invariant: INV-14
file: pem_files.c
catches: pem_files_test
reason: ch_p256_key_from_pem stops checking its cpu value, so a device
  object, which defines no bit, takes any value, and a host object takes
  a value without CH_CPU_PROBED or with a bit it does not define. The
  ruling holds the call to init's rule (docs/decisions.md 131).
  test_key_cpu passes 1, the top bit and every bit to a device object and
  requires CH_EINVAL.

--- old
    int ok = cpu_value_ok(cpu) && pem_len <= CH_PEM_KEY_TEXT_MAX &&
--- new
    int ok = pem_len <= CH_PEM_KEY_TEXT_MAX &&
